    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122992": {
      "title": "Lecturer of Italian",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Lecturer of Italian Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Lecturer of Italian Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG72 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Lecturer of Italian Department Languages and Intercultural Studies Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The Department of Languages and Intercultural Studies at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a full-time lecturer of Italian to begin August 16, 2027. This position is benefit eligible. The successful candidate will be able to teach all levels of Italian language as well as occasional English-language courses in our Intercultural Studies program. We are particularly interested in candidates with experience or interest in language pedagogy. Candidates’ application materials should provide evidence of the candidate’s ability to contribute to a multi-language department that values a variety of perspectives. The teaching load for this position is 30 credits per year (approximately equivalent to a 5-5 load). Required qualifications include a master’s degree in Italian, Italian Studies, or a closely related field; experience teaching language and culture courses to students from a broad range of majors at a US institution of higher education; native or near-native fluency in Italian and English; and experience teaching with technology. Preferred qualifications include evidence of exceptional teaching, evidence of interest in ongoing professional development, evidence of familiarity with ACTFL Standards, and demonstrable experience in languages for the professions. Interested candidates should submit a CV, copy of transcripts, a cover letter 