    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122989": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Management",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor of Management Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Assistant/Associate Professor of Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG74 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Management Department Management & Decision Sciences Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The E. Craig Wall Sr. College of Business Administration at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a nine-month, full-time tenure-track position in Management at the Assistant/Associate Professor level beginning Fall 2027. The Wall College of Business ascribes to the teacher-scholar model that prioritizes excellent teaching supported by ongoing scholarly engagement and service. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to teaching excellence and student engagement through experiential learning and will maintain ongoing scholarly engagement to support academic currency. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in the area of human resource management, organizational behavior, leadership, and principles of management. Teaching expectations are typically three courses per semester, and may include face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online deliveries In addition to teaching responsibilities, engagement in scholarship is required. Candidates should demonstrate recent scholarly engagement (e.g., peer reviewed publications, conference presentations, or other scholarly activity) consistent with expectations for maintaining academic qualification under AACSB standards. The individual will also be responsible for contributing to the assessment of student learning outcomes and engaging in other service activities within the department, college, campus, community, and profession. The candidate must have a Ph.D. or D.B.A. from an AACSB -accredited institution in management or a related discipline. A.B.D.s with a clear plan for completion by December 31, 2027 will be considered. Applicants must demonstrate abilities, skills, and enthusiasm consistent with teaching excellence and instructional innovation. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. Accredited by AACSB International, the Wall College of Business serves more than 3000 graduate and undergraduate students and has faculty members represented by seven academic disciplines: Accounting, Commercial and Investment Real Estate, Economics, Finance, Management and Decision Sciences, Marketing, and Hospitality and Resort Tourism Management, as well as graduate programs in Business Administration ( MBA ) and Masters in Finance. The Wall College of Business has a WRDS platform with access to CRSP , Compustat, and Datastream to support quality scholarship and teaching. Regional outreach is accomplished through activities of the Center for Real Estate and Economic Development, the Clay Brittain Jr. Center for Resort Tourism, the Community and Business Engagement Institute, and others. Additional information about the College and the University, including its programs, can be obtained from the University’s website (http://www.coastal.edu). The Department of Management and Decision Sciences houses a major in management with concentration options in entrepreneurial management, human resource management, international management, operations and supply chain management, general management, and organizational leadership. The management major is the largest at the University, with enrollment of over 1,000 students. The department also supports the MBA program and the business core curriculum. Interested candidates should electronically submit at https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122937 the following documents: 1) a letter of application, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) statement on teaching philosophy, 4) copies of the most recent student evaluations of teaching, 5) unofficial graduate transcripts, and 6) names and contact information for three professional references. Review of applications will begin by November 19, 2026 and continue until position is filled. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications PhD or DBA in management or a closely related field from an AACSB or regionally-accredited institution. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities This position communicates (express or exchange information) with students to provide instruction. Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00521P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/19/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122937 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom, laboratory, and/or studio. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Conducts research to create and add to knowledge in a field or produces creative work. Trains students in related research techniques and in creative production. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD/DBA in management or a closely related field? Yes, already have Yes, will have by appointment start date No If you are currently completing a PhD/DBA, please list your anticipated graduation date (month, year). (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Statement of Teaching Philosophy Teaching Evaluation(s) Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
