    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122965": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Global, Transnational, or World History",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Assistant Professor of Global, Transnational, or World History Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Assistant Professor of Global, Transnational, or World History Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG74 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Assistant Professor of Global, Transnational, or World History Department History Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The Department of History in the Edwards College of Humanities and Fine Arts at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a tenure-track position as an Assistant Professor of Global, Transnational, or World History, beginning in August 2027. We seek candidates who demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and research, the potential for excellence in graduate instruction, and the pursuit of an active scholarly agenda. Applicants with specialization in the early-modern and/or modern periods and an interest outside of the US are particularly encouraged to apply. The desired candidate will hold a Ph.D. in history by the time of appointment with a focus on themes relevant to the department. Applicants that can contribute to the development of our curricular initiatives in the history of science & technology, the environment, and/or applied history as well as supplement the History Department’s Social Studies major and/or the Peace and Conflict Studies and/or War and Society minors, and/or the College’s regional minors are particularly welcome to apply. The successful candidate will teach 6 courses per year: a combination of world history or thematic survey courses and upper-level courses in their area(s) of specialization, per the needs of the department and in consultation with the Department Chair. Interested candidates must apply online at https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122865 . A complete set of application materials must include: a letter of application describing the candidate’s interest, qualifications, teaching experience, and scholarly agenda; at least 2 sample syllabi (1 survey class and 1 potential upper-level class); an unofficial graduate transcript; curriculum vitae; and the names and contact information of three references. A review of applications will begin on November 12, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00516P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/12/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122865 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom, laboratory, and/or studio. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Conducts research to create and add to knowledge in a field or produces creative work. Trains students in related research techniques and in creative production. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Performs other departmental needs as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122960": {
      "title": "Associate Professor/Professor/Chair of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Associate Professor/Professor/Chair of Health Sciences Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Associate Professor/Professor/Chair of Health Sciences Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG75 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Associate Professor/Professor/Chair of Health Sciences Department CMC College of HHP Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The Conway Medical Center College of Health and Human Performance at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for the position of Department Chair/Associate Professor/Professor for the newly formed Department of Health Sciences, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. We seek a collaborative, conscientious, and strategic leader and communicator, with a demonstrated commitment to faculty and student success. This is a 9-month tenured faculty appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor rank, with additional summer responsibilities and administrative compensation. Minimum Qualifications · A terminal degree (Ph.D. DrPH, or Ed.D.) in a Health Sciences or Public Health related field. · A sustained record of scholarly research and publication in quality peer-reviewed journals. · Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the undergraduate and/or graduate level. Preferred Qualifications · A record of building internal and external partnerships. · Prior administrative or leadership experience in an academic setting strongly preferred. · Experience working with external partners within the healthcare industry. · Experience pursuing and securing external grants and funding. · A track record of innovative and strategic academic program development at undergraduate and graduate levels. · Familiarity working within and across different Health Sciences subdisciplines, such as Public Health, Health Administration, and other allied health professions. · A strong record of effective communication and visibility in internal and external settings. · Evidence of effective collaboration and coalition-building that increases faculty and student success. The Chair responsibilities will include a 2-2 teaching load (all subdisciplines in Health Sciences are encouraged to apply) and lead the department in the following areas: Providing academic and administrative leadership, Recruiting, mentoring, and evaluating faculty, Overseeing course scheduling and instructional quality. Managing departmental budgets and allocating faculty development resources. Leading curriculum and new program development and revisions. Overseeing program assessment, and accreditation efforts. Addressing student concerns and supporting student success. Representing the department within the college and university and Fostering partnerships with external and community stakeholders. The Conway Medical Center College of Health and Human Performance serves more than 2100 undergraduate and graduate students through the Departments of Health Sciences, Kinesiology, Nursing, and Recreation and Sport Management. The College is one the institution’s fastest growing colleges and is targeted for continued development that supports increased student opportunities, faculty growth, workforce development, community engagement, and external partnerships. In support of its mission, the College will move into its new academic home in Fall, 2028. Interested candidates should submit: a letter of application, current curriculum vitae, copies of transcripts of all graduate work (copies are acceptable at this time), and contact information for least three (3) professional references. All information and material must be submitted electronically at: https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122930 . Applicants that are invited for interviews must provide official transcripts of all graduate coursework prior to visiting campus. A review of applications will begin on November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Current knowledge and mastery of demonstrable skills in area of expertise with ability and willingness to effectively communicate them to students and colleagues is required. Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00518P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/16/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122930 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom, laboratory, and/or studio. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University Catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Conducts research to create and add to knowledge in a field or produces creative work. Trains students in related research techniques and in creative production. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
