    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122879": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Assistant Professor – Mechanical Engineering Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Assistant Professor – Mechanical Engineering Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG74 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Assistant Professor – Mechanical Engineering Department Engineering Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The Department of Engineering Science in the Gupta College of Science and Engineering at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level beginning Fall 2027 in support of its Engineering Science program. Applicants must have a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Proven expertise and research interests in the field of Biomedical instrumentations and/or Materials Science are required. Special preference will be given to applicants with interdisciplinary qualifications or experience. Applicants must be teacher-scholars who will establish research agendas that involve undergraduate students and teach introductory engineering courses, as well as upper-level courses in their area of expertise. The position also requires engaging engineering students through active advising and mentoring of extracurricular groups. Start-up funds will be available to establish a research agenda that incorporates undergraduate students. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The Gupta College of Science and Engineering works to provide a premier and experience-driven STEM education to all of its students. The college’s approach weaves together a strong liberal arts core, engaged STEM pedagogy, and high-impact practices associated with experiential learning to provide the highest quality STEM education possible. As one of the largest colleges at the University, Gupta College of Science and Engineering offers an impressive array of distinctive undergraduate degree programs, focused concentrations, and minors along with master’s and doctoral degree programs. The college is committed to providing students and faculty with cutting-edge scientific equipment, instrumentation, and marine vessels for both teaching and research purposes. The Burroughs and Chapin Center for Marine and Wetland Studies within the Gupta College of Science and Engineering also offers the potential for collaboration with faculty engaged in related coastal and marine research issues. Interested candidates in this opportunity or any other position they feel qualified for should submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references electronically at https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122788 . One reference must be able to address the applicant’s teaching ability. Candidates must also submit a two-page research agenda that emphasizes the potential for undergraduate participation and a two-page statement of teaching philosophy that describes specifics of what a typical class session would look like to an outside observer. Screening of applications will begin on November 6, 2026 and continue until position is filled. Inquiries about the positions should be directed to Roi Gurka by email to rgurka@coastal.edu . The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications Post-doctoral experience is preferred. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Current knowledge and mastery of demonstrable skills in area of expertise with ability and willingness to effectively communicate them to students and colleagues is required. Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00510P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122788 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom and/or laboratory. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Conducts research to create and add knowledge in a field, including the advancement of new theories and principles to improve educational effectiveness. Trains students in related research techniques. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122877": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counselor Education",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Assistant Professor of Counselor Education Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Assistant Professor of Counselor Education Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG74 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Assistant Professor of Counselor Education Department Education Sciences and Organizations Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The Spadoni College of Education and Social Sciences at Coastal Carolina University announces a full-time tenure track position in Counselor Education beginning August 2027. The M.Ed. in Counseling Program includes both Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling specialization areas. The successful candidate will teach graduate counseling courses within the M.Ed. in Counseling Program using both in-person and virtual modalities, provide clinical supervision for School Counseling and Clinical Mental Health Counseling internship students, advise graduate students, participate in scholarship and professional service, contribute to assessment and continuous improvement initiatives, and support the program’s pursuit and maintenance of CACREP accreditation. The faculty member will collaborate closely with program faculty and community partners while contributing to the preparation of ethical, culturally responsive, and clinically competent professional counselors. The faculty and administrators in the Spadoni College, along with professional staff across the University, will provide meaningful support for the successful candidate’s teaching and scholarship as elements of their personal and professional career development. The Spadoni College administration encourages each faculty member to grow professionally, and supports a healthy work-life integration. Required Qualifications: · Earned doctoral degree in Counselor Education, preferably from a CACREP -accredited program, or qualifications meeting one of the alternative core counselor education faculty eligibility pathways specified in CACREP 2024 Standard 1.Y, by the appointment date. · Professional identity as a counselor educator · Professional experience as a P–12 School Counselor and/or Clinical Mental Health Counselor · Current professional counseling licensure and eligibility for South Carolina licensure · Experience providing counseling supervision · Demonstrated potential for excellence in graduate teaching · Ability to teach graduate counseling courses using synchronous and asynchronous online instructional modalities Preferred Qualifications: · Professional experience as both a P–12 School Counselor and Clinical Mental Health Counselor · Approved Clinical Supervisor ( ACS ) credential or equivalent · Experience teaching in CACREP -aligned counselor education programs · Experience with practicum and internship supervision · Experience with CACREP accreditation, assessment, curriculum development, or program evaluation · Experience with online counselor education · Record of scholarly publications and presentations · Experience developing community partnerships and clinical training sites Interested candidates should submit: · a letter of application (outlining interest in the position and specifying how the candidate meets the required and preferred qualifications), · current curriculum vitae, · copies of transcripts of all graduate work (copies are acceptable at this time), · Counselor Education Teaching Philosophy · Research Statement · and a list of at least three professional references. All information and material must be submitted electronically. Applicants that are invited for interviews must provide official transcripts of all undergraduate and graduate work prior to visiting campus. Review of applications and materials will begin on November 6, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please visit here to apply: https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122698 . Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications 1. Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision by the appointment date.; 2. Professional identity as a counselor educator.; 3. Professional experience as a P–12 School Counselor.; 4. Professional preparation and experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling.; 5. Current professional counseling licensure and eligibility for South Carolina licensure.; 6. Experience providing counseling supervision. Preferred Qualifications 1. Doctorate from a CACREP -accredited Counselor Education and Supervision program.; 2. Approved Clinical Supervisor ( ACS ) credential or equivalent.; 3. Experience teaching in CACREP -aligned counselor education programs.; 4. Experience with practicum and internship supervision.; 5. Experience with CACREP accreditation, assessment, curriculum development, or program evaluation.; 6. Experience with online counselor education.; 7. Record of scholarly publications and presentations.; 8. Experience developing community partnerships and clinical training sites Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated potential for excellence in graduate teaching; Ability to teach graduate counseling courses effectively in-person and virtually using synchronous and asynchronous instructional methods; Knowledge of counselor education and CACREP standards; Knowledge of Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling practice; Knowledge of counseling ethics and supervision. Strong communication, collaboration, mentoring, and interpersonal skills; Ability to contribute to scholarship, accreditation, curriculum development, and program assessment; Ability to build collaborative relationships with community partners and clinical sites. Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00507P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122698 Job Duties Job Duty Teach graduate counseling courses in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling in-person and virtually using synchronous and asynchronous instructional methods. Job Duty Provide individual, triadic, and group supervision for practicum and internship students; advise and mentor graduate students; and evaluate student clinical competencies in accordance with CACREP standards. Job Duty Engage in scholarship appropriate for a tenure-track appointment through research, publications, presentations, grant activity, and/or professional engagement while maintaining an active scholarly agenda. Job Duty Participate in program assessment, curriculum development, Annual Program Evaluation, CACREP accreditation activities, recruitment, admissions, and university, college, departmental, and professional service. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
