    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122716": {
      "title": "Nursing Clinical Instructor -Teaching Associate",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Nursing Clinical Instructor -Teaching Associate Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Nursing Clinical Instructor -Teaching Associate Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Employer-based sponsorship is not available for this position. Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Details Posting Summary Internal Title Nursing Clinical Instructor -Teaching Associate Department Nursing and Health Sciences Position Type TFAC - Temporary Faculty Full or Part Time Basis Job Details Coastal Carolina University, Department of Nursing and Health Sciences, within the Conway Medical Center College of Health and Human Performance, is seeking applications for two nursing clinical instructor vacancies with a primary focus in clinical, simulation and/or laboratory instruction. These positions will address instructional needs in the Nursing and Health Sciences Department, starting in January 2027. Successful candidates will play a crucial role in educating undergraduate students in clinical and laboratory settings, in particular mental health clinical settings and other settings as needed. Candidates must possess a minimum of a bachelors (or higher) degree in nursing, hold an unencumbered active license as a registered nurse in South Carolina or another Compact state, have a minimum of two years of clinical experience as a registered or advanced practice nurse related to the primary area of responsibility. Preferred qualifications include a record of clinical or laboratory teaching, experience in instructional settings, and experience working with nursing students. Candidates should complete the online application and submit a letter of application, a current CV, copies of all transcripts, proof of current RN licensure, contact information for three references and statement of clinical teaching experience/teaching philosophy. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Additional comments regarding this position Posting Detail Information Posting Number TA00557P Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) 05/15/2027 Job Open Date 09/18/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Employer-based sponsorship is not available for this position. Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122583 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
