    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122197": {
      "title": "Teaching Associate - Dance",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Teaching Associate - Dance Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Teaching Associate - Dance Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Internal Title Teaching Associate - Dance Department Theatre Position Type TFAC - Temporary Faculty Full or Part Time Basis Job Details The Department of Theatre at Coastal Carolina University, accredited by the National Association of Schools of Theatre ( NAST ), invites applications for part-time employment in the Theatre Department as a Teaching associate of dance. This position has a potential start date of August 16th, 2026, or January 4th, 2027. The department offers a B.F.A degree in Theatre Arts (audition/interview only) with concentrations in Acting, Musical Theatre, Physical Theatre, and Design and Production, a B.A. degree in Theatre, and Minors in Dance and Theatre. The program seeks highly qualified individuals who will support the continued advancement of the program and especially the growing Dance Minor. This highly collaborative department maintains an ambitious production season, in addition to new works and staged readings to connect students with working professionals. Department faculty maintain professional careers in their respective disciplines. Senior B.F.A. performance students participate in a New York Showcase for industry professionals, senior B.F.A. design/production showcase their portfolios at national conferences, and students in our department can study abroad in collaboration with our conservatory partner, Theatre Academy London. The Department of Theatre seeks applications for a pool of qualified adjunct faculty to teach undergraduate dance courses on a semester-by-semester basis, contingent upon departmental needs. Successful candidates may be assigned one or more courses in areas including, but not limited to, ballet, modern, jazz, tap, contemporary, musical theatre dance, choreography, movement, dance appreciation, dance history, and other specialized areas consistent with the candidate’s training and professional experience. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. To be qualified for this position, applicants must have completed at least 18 graduate credit hours in Dance or a closely related discipline. Possessing a master’s degree, MFA , or other appropriate graduate degree in Dance, Choreography, Performance, or a related field is preferred. Preference also will be given to candidates with successful college-level teaching experience and/or substantial professional experience in dance performance, choreography, movement direction, or dance education. The department welcomes applicants who demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student mentorship, and inclusive learning environments that support students from diverse backgrounds and experiences. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue throughout the academic year as instructional needs arise. Interested candidates should submit their application materials electronically at [include link here]. A complete application should include an online application, cover letter, curriculum vitae or professional résumé, unofficial transcripts, and contact information for three professional references. References may be contacted if a teaching opportunity becomes available. Compensation is competitive and based on qualifications and assigned teaching load. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Additional comments regarding this position Posting Detail Information Posting Number TA00539P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2026 Position End Date (if temporary) 12/15/2026 Job Open Date 07/06/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122112 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
