    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122080": {
      "title": "Dean of the Graduate School at Coastal Carolina University",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Dean of the Graduate School at Coastal Carolina University Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Dean of the Graduate School at Coastal Carolina University Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. To Apply: A confidential review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position has been filled. For full consideration, individuals are encouraged to apply by August 17, 2026 . Please submit PDF versions of your curriculum vitae and of your letter of interest. Note: there is flexibility regarding the start date for the position, likely January 2027 or summer 2027. To Apply Online: https://theapplicantmanager.com/jobs?pos=su511 Chris Shade Senior Consultant Summit Search Solutions, Inc. 440-655-2285 cshade@summitsearchsolutions.com Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UD09 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Dean of the Graduate School at Coastal Carolina University Department College of Graduate and Continuing Studies Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 12 mo. Job Details Coastal Carolina University seeks a Dean of the Graduate School Click here to view position profile: https://summitsearchsolutions.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/CCU_DeanGradSchool_Profile.pdf Location: Conway, South Carolina The Position: The next Dean of the Graduate School at Coastal Carolina University will be an experienced individual who will provide vision, direction, and leadership to define and build this new academic unit. The Dean will report to the Provost and Vice President of Academic Affairs and serve as a member of the Provost’s leadership team and a strategic partner in shaping graduate education across the institution. The Dean will oversee a team of five (5) including the Associate Dean, Graduate and Special Populations Enrollment Coordinator, Administrative Coordinator/Budget Manager, Marketing Coordinator, and Student Success Coordinator. Responsibilities: Provide strategic leadership for the Graduate School, advancing a vision aligned with university priorities for graduate enrollment growth, student success, academic quality, and institutional advancement. Lead the expansion and refinement of master’s and doctoral program portfolios using data-informed, market-responsive strategies that reflect workforce demand, regional needs, and CCU’s academic strengths. Champion the development and quality of in-person, online and hybrid graduate programs, ensuring appropriate academic standards, student support systems, and sustainable faculty workload models. Serve as a collaborative, service-oriented partner to academic colleges, building strong relationships with deans, chairs, and faculty while establishing centralized policies, processes, and administrative support structures. Advocate for graduate students and enhance enrollment strategy by partnering with enrollment management on recruitment, marketing, and yield efforts, while ensuring graduate student needs are represented in campus-wide planning and services. Strengthen the role of graduate education in supporting research productivity and doctoral culture, collaborating with academic colleges and research leadership to advance research goals. Required Qualifications Qualifications: An eared doctorate from an accredited institution. A history of demonstrated achievement in furthering the role of graduate education at a university. Experience of administrative leadership in graduate education, including program planning and development, assessment, new program approval, budgeting, student support, and/or enrollment management. History of collaboration with deans and faculty colleagues to cultivate and grow graduate programming and enrollment. Experience related to fiscal and budgetary management related to graduate education including budgeting, revenue and cost projections, enrollment targets, and support. Ability to grow online programs, particularly master’s programs in high workforce needs areas. Experience with PhD programs and ability to foster their success. Experience managing people and the ability to facilitate teamwork among faculty, staff, and students. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Posting Designation Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00497P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 01/04/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 06/24/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To Apply: A confidential review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position has been filled. For full consideration, individuals are encouraged to apply by August 17, 2026 . Please submit PDF versions of your curriculum vitae and of your letter of interest. Note: there is flexibility regarding the start date for the position, likely January 2027 or summer 2027. To Apply Online: https://theapplicantmanager.com/jobs?pos=su511 Chris Shade Senior Consultant Summit Search Solutions, Inc. 440-655-2285 cshade@summitsearchsolutions.com Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122079 Job Duties Job Duty Develops and implements a College budget. Job Duty Supervises faculty and staff. Recommends matters relating to faculty appointments, retention, salaries, promotion, and termination. Job Duty Develops academic programs that advance the mission of the University. Works with department chairs to plan course offerings. Job Duty Oversees academic advising and other initiatives to increase student engagement and retention. Evaluates and certifies students? degree requirements. Job Duty Develops external relationship and increases philanthropic giving. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned by the Provost. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/123043": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG74 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Marketing Department Marketing & Hospitality, Resort, & Tourism Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details The E. Craig Wall Sr. College of Business Administration at Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level in the Department of Marketing and Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management, beginning Fall 2027. To be considered, candidates should hold a Ph.D. in Marketing from an AACSB -accredited institution. A.B.D. candidates with a clear plan for degree completion by December 2027 are also encouraged to apply. A candidate with a completed Ph.D. must have a recent and consistent record of publication in quality refereed journals. Applicants must demonstrate abilities, skills, and enthusiasm consistent with teaching excellence and instructional innovation and consistent with the Wall College of Business mission. The Department also values candidates with industry experience and community engagement. The individual hired for this position will have responsibilities in teaching, research, and service. The successful candidate should have experience and expertise in teaching Marketing Research and Marketing Analytics, along with one or more marketing courses at the undergraduate or master’s level. Candidates with expertise in emerging technologies (e.g., artificial intelligence, virtual reality, augmented reality, mixed reality) and their applications in marketing are especially encouraged to apply. The teaching load is typically three courses per semester and may include face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online delivery methods. In addition to teaching responsibilities, active engagement in scholarly research is required. The individual hired will also be responsible for contributing to assessment of student learning outcomes and engaging in service activities within the department, college, campus, community, and profession. Accredited by AACSB International, the Wall College of Business serves more than 3,000 graduate and undergraduate students. The college offers undergraduate majors in seven disciplines (Accounting, Commercial and Investment Real Estate Economics, Finance, Management, Marketing, Hospitality and Tourism Management), as well as MBA and Master of Science in Finance degree programs. Additional information about the College and the University and its programs can be obtained by accessing the university’s website ( http://www.coastal.edu ). The Department of Marketing and Hospitality, Resort, and Tourism Management houses majors and minors in both areas. The Marketing major emphasizes consumer decision making, research methodology and data analysis, and the identification of and response to marketing problems and opportunities. The Wall College of Business also houses a behavioral research lab to support quality scholarship and teaching in Marketing and other disciplines. Interested candidates should submit: 1) a letter of application, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) copies of the most recent student evaluations of teaching, 4) a research statement, 5) a statement of teaching philosophy, 6) unofficial graduate transcripts, and 7) names and contact information for three professional references electronically to: https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122940 . Review of application materials will begin November 16, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications PhD or DBA in marketing or a closely related field from an AACSB or regionally-accredited institution. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities This position communicates (express or exchange information) with students to provide instruction. Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? Yes Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship may be considered for this position, subject to institutional review and applicable law. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00523P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/16/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/122940 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom, laboratory, and/or studio. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Conducts research to create and add to knowledge in a field or produces creative work. Trains students in related research techniques and in creative production. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD/DBA in marketing or a related discipline or a different field? Yes, already have Yes, will have by appointment start date No If you are currently completing a PhD/DBA, please list your anticipated graduation date (month, year). (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Statement of Teaching Philosophy Research Statement Teaching Evaluation(s) Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/123042": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Journalism",
      "description": "Coastal Carolina University Portal | Lecturer in Journalism Skip to Main Content Coastal Carolina University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help State Pay Grades www.coastal.edu Lecturer in Journalism Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Summary Classification Code UG72 Pay Grade 0 Subject to Drug/Alcohol Testing Guidelines No Subject to Credit Check No Internal Title Lecturer in Journalism Department Communication, Media, and Culture Position Type PFAC - Slotted Faculty Full or Part Time Full-Time Basis 9 mo. Job Details Coastal Carolina University invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track lecturer position in Journalism to begin August 2027. Candidates must hold a master’s or terminal degree in Journalism, Communication, Mass Communication, Media Arts or a related field by the date of appointment. The Department of Communication, Media and Culture offers majors in Communication, Journalism & Sports Media, and Public Relations & Strategic Communication. The teaching load is five courses per academic semester and may include face-to-face, hybrid or distance learning deliveries. Teaching assignments may include evening or weekend courses. We are seeking an excellent teacher-practitioner to teach the department’s foundation courses in journalism, such as news writing and reporting, media writing and multimedia storytelling. The successful candidate will also teach courses in their area of expertise, which should align with current departmental majors, minors and course offerings. Preferred qualifications include professional experience in news or sports reporting for broadcast, digital or print media outlets; the ability to teach multimedia and multiplatform journalism; and college-level teaching experience. Expertise in areas such as broadcast newswriting and producing, digital content producing, multimedia newswriting, data or investigative reporting, or artificial intelligence in the newsroom is welcome. Interested candidates should submit: (1) a letter of application addressing the qualifications above and describing teaching experience or ability, (2) curriculum vitae with links to a portfolio of professional work, (3) unofficial graduate transcripts, (4) evidence of teaching effectiveness, such as sample syllabi or student evaluations, if available, and (5) the names and contact information for three references electronically at https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/123031 . Official transcripts and letters of reference may be requested for interviewed candidates. Review of application materials will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information or questions, contact associate professor Adam Pitluk, PhD, at apitluk@coastal.edu . Coastal Carolina University is a public comprehensive liberal arts institution located in Conway, South Carolina, just nine miles from the Atlantic coastal resort city of Myrtle Beach. Coastal Carolina University enrolls over 12,000 students from 48 states and 53 nations. The University is accredited by the Southern Association of Colleges and Schools Commission on Colleges to award the baccalaureate and master’s degrees of national and/or regional significance in the arts and sciences, business, humanities, education, and health and human services, a specialist degree in instructional technology, and PhD degrees in marine science: coastal and marine systems science and education sciences. The University provides equal employment opportunity without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, citizenship status, national origin, or because an employee or applicant for employment is an individual with a disability or a disabled veteran, an Armed Forces service medal veteran, a recently separated veteran, or an active-duty wartime or campaign badge veteran, or other “protected veteran,” as defined by law. Coastal Carolina University is an EO/AA employer. Required Qualifications Must hold the appropriate terminal degree or meet the established alternative qualifications, and exhibit strong potential for excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Posting Sponsorship Designation Will Employer-based sponsorship be considered for this position? No Posting Designation Employer-based sponsorship is not available for this position. Work Authorization & Sponsorship for Job Posting Employment at Coastal Carolina University is contingent upon authorization to work in the United States. CCU may consider employer-based visa sponsorship for certain positions; however, sponsorship is discretionary, not guaranteed, and subject to legal, financial, and institutional requirements. CCU rarely sponsors part-time, temporary, staff or non-tenure-track roles and will not sponsor H-1B petitions when the federally required $100,000 fee applies. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F00525P Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 08/16/2027 Position End Date (if temporary) Job Open Date 10/27/2026 Job Close Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.coastal.edu/postings/123031 Job Duties Job Duty Teaches students in the classroom, laboratory, and/or studio. Job Duty Prepares content, syllabi, and University Moodle/curricular site for each course and/or lab assigned each semester. Communicates to students after reviewing assignments. Calculates and assigns grades (e.g., mid-term and final) through established procedures listed in the Faculty Manual and University catalog. Tracks and reports absences as directed by the Office of the Registrar. Job Duty Posts and holds regular office hours each week per College and University guidelines. Engages in University-related activities including committee assignments, meetings, ceremonies, events and scholarly pursuits as prescribed in the Faculty Manual. Job Duty Performs other duties as assigned. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Application Transcripts Curriculum Vitae Reference List Optional Documents Other Document 1 Other Document 2 Other Document 3 About CCU Academics Admissions & Aid Athletics Campus Life Services & Support Site Privacy Policy Contact Us © 2025 Coastal Carolina University Coastal Carolina University prohibits any form of discrimination against its students, faculty, staff and applicants in its programs or for admission to or employment with the University. For more information, visit Title IX or EEO. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
